          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Storm Surge (Maximum Scale)": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "高潮浸水想定（想定最大規模）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Storm Surge and Tsunami": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "高潮・津波"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Storm surge can also happen when it isn't high tide.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "満潮の時刻でなくても高潮は起こります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Storm surge information uses the same alert levels. Leave early, and by Alert Level 4 at the latest.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "高潮の情報も同じ警戒レベルで発表されます。早めに、遅くとも警戒レベル4までに避難します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Terms of Use (GSI)": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "国土地理院コンテンツ利用規約"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Terms of Use (PDL1.0)": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "利用規約（PDL1.0）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "This data is updated from time to time.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "本データは随時更新されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "This data is what each municipality registered for the sites and shelters its mayor designated under the Basic Act on Disaster Management. It may be out of date or incomplete, so always check the latest details with the municipality.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "本データは、災害対策基本法第49条の4・第49条の7に基づき市町村長が指定した指定緊急避難場所・指定避難所の情報を各市町村に登録いただいたものです。なお、最新でない場合や未掲載の場合があるため、最新かつ詳細の状況などは必ず当該市町村にご確認ください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "To use a PIN, press 3 to record or 4 to play.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "暗証番号を使うときは、録音は3、再生は4を押します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tohoku": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "東北"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tsunami": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "津波"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tsunami (Inundation Depth)": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "津波浸水想定（浸水深）"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Update": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "更新"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Useful Resources": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "役立つ情報"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Volcanic Alert Levels: 1 be aware the volcano is active, 2 keep away from the crater, 3 keep off the mountain, 4 older people evacuate, 5 evacuate.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "噴火警戒レベル：1 活火山であることに留意、2 火口周辺規制、3 入山規制、4 高齢者等避難、5 避難。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Volcanic Event": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "火山現象"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Warning signs: cracks in a slope or the ground, small stones falling, rumbling from the hillside, muddy river or well water, and a river that drops while rain continues.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "前ぶれ：がけや地面のひび割れ、小石の落下、山鳴りや地鳴り、川や井戸の水のにごり、雨が続いているのに下がる川の水位。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Warnings and Monitoring": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "警報・観測"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Waves arrive more than once, and later waves can be higher.": {
      "localizations": {
